  "root_node": "source.raw.lineitem",
  "cause": "upstream_data",
  "action": "escalate",
  "evidence": "The failing dbt checks not_null_stg_lineitem_order_key and not_null_stg_lineitem_order_line_id report 1550 rows with null values. Inspection of raw.lineitem shows 1550 rows where l_orderkey is NULL (SELECT COUNT(*) ... shows null_orderkey = 1550). Since stg_lineitem simply forwards l_orderkey (and uses it to build order_line_id), the nulls originate in the source raw table. No downstream model logic is at fault; the source data is missing required order keys. Therefore the incident is caused by upstream data and should be escalated to the source owner."
}
